  "query_preview": "(Sunday through Wednesday)...\nThe Extreme Heat Warning for the deserts and Heat Advisory for the\nmountains and Inland Empire has been extended through Sunday with\nonly a slight decline in HeatRisk on Sunday. Greater declines are\nexpected for Monday and Tuesday with moderate HeatRisk for next\nTuesday confined mostly to the deserts.\n\nEnsemble output shows another peak in precipitable water values\nfor Sunday afternoon, similar to the peak for this afternoon, then\na gradual slow decline through next week. A slight chance for\nafternoon showers and thunderstorms for the mountains will\ncontinue for Sunday through Tuesday with gradual cooling and\ndrying for the rest of next week. For Thursday of next week, high\ntemperatures for the deserts and near the coast will be around\naverage and could be as much as 4 to 8 degrees below average for\nthe inland valleys. For Thursday of next week, high temperatures\ncould range from the 70s near the coast to the mid 80s to mid 90s\nfor the Inland Empire with 106 to 110 for the lower deserts.",
